                  <items count="8">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A panel for custom notes and String values</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">73482535-31ad-40be-80e1-2e53983b1047</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Instructions</item>
                    <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="ScrollRatio" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">0</item>
                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Squid draws a bitmap with a list of instructions.

If your instructions are collected in a data tree, the data tree gets flattened internally.
It means that one Squid component can draw one bitmap at a time, using only one rectangle. 
If you input more than one bitmap rectangle, Squid will use the first one.

Instructions are listed in the Instructions panel.</item>
                  </items>
